Description: drm: Keep a stereo pair's commit on one commit thread
 The commit of a stereo pair went to the commit thread of whichever
 output presented first, and its page flip made both pipelines' commit
 threads release their committed commit. With the order of the outputs
 changing from frame to frame, one thread could have the next commit in
 flight when the other thread's commit flipped, and that page flip freed
 it. Its own page-flip event then reached freed memory and KWin crashed
 in DrmGpu::pageFlipHandler(), usually within seconds of pairing two
 outputs.
 .
 Always give the pair's commit to the thread of the output whose UUID
 sorts first, and let a pair's page flip release only that commit.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/kwin/commit/3ca10c931d7923631cbd182b5424d1f5f88e8c08
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
